    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37117" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porrīgo</span></b> , ĭnis,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the scurf</i>, <i>dandruff</i> on the head,
				<i><span class="en">Cels. 6,
				2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 6, 23, § 53</span></i>; <i><span class="en">20, 6, 27, §
			69</span></i>; <i><span class="en">28, 11, 46,
				§ 163</span></i>; 32, 4, 14, § 35; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				3, 126</span></i>.—Also of other hairy parts of the body,
				<i><span class="en">Scrib. Larg. 243</span></i>.—Of animals,
			perhaps <i>the mange</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porci,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 2,
					80</span></i>
			.</div>
